&lt;h1 class="relative group">Who Is Our Enemy?
&lt;div id="who-is-our-enemy" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#who-is-our-enemy" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h1>
&lt;p>We use the words &lt;strong>friend&lt;/strong> and &lt;strong>enemy&lt;/strong> very easily.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Someone supports what I want to do:&lt;/p>
&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>He is my friend.&lt;/p>&lt;/blockquote>
&lt;p>Someone opposes me:&lt;/p>
&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>He is my enemy.&lt;/p>&lt;/blockquote>
&lt;p>Someone remains silent when I expect support:&lt;/p>
&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>He is not really my friend.&lt;/p>&lt;/blockquote>
&lt;p>But is it so simple?&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Desire Renunciation And A Limited Self</title><link>https://dasarpai.github.io/wiaposts/desire-renunciation-and-a-limited-self/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 Aug 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hari@dasarpai.com (Dr. Hari Thapliyaal)</author><guid>https://dasarpai.github.io/wiaposts/desire-renunciation-and-a-limited-self/</guid><description>&lt;p>
&lt;figure>
&lt;img class="my-0 rounded-md" loading="lazy" src="https://dasarpai.github.io/assets/images/wiapost/5104-Desire-Renunciation-And-A-Limited-Self.jpg" alt="Desire Renunciation And A Limited Self" />
&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;h1 class="relative group">Desire Renunciation And A Limited Self
&lt;div id="desire-renunciation-and-a-limited-self" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#desire-renunciation-and-a-limited-self" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h1>
&lt;p>We know without desire living is not possible.&lt;br>
It amazes me the way&lt;br>
the concept of desirelessness&lt;br>
has been taught and understood in our society.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>We know a desire and dreams&lt;br>
helps human moving in his life&lt;br>
With desire human eat, drink and walk,&lt;br>
With desire human talk, dance and sing,&lt;br>
With desire human search, paint, and construct.&lt;br>
With the desire, we want to live and die!&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>